Subject: [PATCH 7/16] Keep agy's project check and guard hooks working

Reason: Two places where the local agy integration broke on what agy actually
does. They share a file and no code; each half has its own removal condition.

Project fallback: Since agy 1.3, `--project <id>` for a project agy no longer has (its
record under `~/.gemini/config/projects` is gone) opens `default-cli-project`
instead, exits 0, and still lists the cwd's hooks. The engine's project
check (`/hooks` on the kept id) therefore kept passing, the state file was
never invalidated, and every tool call died at `_grant_permissions` on the
missing record ("Antigravity project record ... is not readable; the tool
project cannot be entitled") with nothing to re-register it. Seen after a
1.2.2 -> 1.3.3 upgrade on 2026-10-13, when FineSub's records were gone.

`_check_project` now reads which project agy opened from the run's own log
(`Conversation using project ID: <id>`). A different id is plain
unavailability, which the project-setup fast path already answers by
registering afresh; right after a registration it fails closed, so a
project agy cannot open never turns into one registration per call. A log
without the line is no verdict: older builds and a missing log behave as
before.

agy 1.4 no longer logs that line for `/hooks`, so the check had nothing to
read again: after 1.4.5 migrated the records on 2026-10-25 and dropped the
tool project's, every tool call died on the missing record once more. The
check now also requires the kept id's record under
`~/.gemini/config/projects`; a missing record is the same unavailability, a
missing records directory is no verdict (agy may have moved it, and only
the tool path needs it).

Guard hook encoding: The PreToolUse guards (`guard_view_file.py`, all three templates)
read their payload with `json.load(sys.stdin)`. agy writes it in UTF-8, but a
text stdin decodes with the locale code page -- cp936 on Chinese Windows.
There a CJK run with an odd number of UTF-8 bytes right before an escaped
quote pairs its last byte with the backslash, the quote closes the string,
and the guard dies with `JSONDecodeError`. agy treats the dead hook as a
refusal, so a correction `submit` whose CSV or task feedback carries
`...不明确\"` is refused and the model rewrites the whole answer. One window
on 2026-10-13 was refused five times (625 s, 790k input tokens); an earlier
run only got through on an all-ASCII `text|text` placeholder answer. The agy
logs show the same failure since 2026-09 on 1.2.2, so it is not agy-version
specific.

`json.loads` on `sys.stdin.buffer.read()` detects UTF-8 itself and never
consults the code page. The script text changes, so each FineSub agy project
re-registers once (its hook digest moves).

Removal: Drop the project-record checks in `_check_project` once upstream
verifies the opened project, or agy fails an unknown `--project` id instead of
falling back. Drop the guard change once upstream's guards read bytes, or agy
stops being the hook writer on Windows. Delete the patch when both halves are
gone.

